# Generated by `boss board --html` — a pure projection of your docs/, re-rendered on
# demand. Committing it means a 200-line diff every time the board moves, for a file
# nobody reads from git.
.boss/board.html

# Copies BOSS keeps of files it was about to overwrite (`boss sync`). Local recovery, not
# project history — and the reason an overwrite is never the end of the story.
.boss/backups/

# Per-person conscience state — stays local, never shared with a cofounder (DEC-001).
# Everything else BOSS writes (docs/ ideas, canvas, decisions, RESUME, and the venture
# brain's read.md) DOES commit — so pushing backs up your thinking AND keeps your
# cofounder in the loop. But the conscience's relationship with YOU — what it said and
# what you did with it — is yours alone; it never travels to a teammate.
.boss/brain/relationship.md
.boss/trace.jsonl

